# Architecture Rules

## Project Structure

Feature-based architecture with auto-discovery. Each feature is self-contained under `src/features/`.

- `src/features/` — Feature modules (auto-discovered at startup)
  - `src/features/steam/` — Steam integration (profile, games, playtime, notifications)
  - `src/features/voice/` — Voice recording
  - `src/features/poll/` — Poll system
  - `src/features/admin/` — Admin commands (admin, settings)
  - `src/features/general/` — General commands (ping, help)
  - `src/features/community/` — Community commands (roulette)
- `src/events/` — Core event handlers (ready, interactionCreate)
- `src/services/` — Shared infrastructure only
  - `src/services/database/` — Connection, transactions, migrations (NO business logic)
  - `src/services/backup/` — Scheduled database backups
  - `src/services/health/` — Health check service
  - `src/services/metrics/` — In-memory metrics
  - `src/services/audit/` — Audit logging orchestration
- `src/handlers/` — Auto-loaders for commands and events
- `src/middleware/` — Pre-execution checks
  - `src/middleware/cooldown/` — Cooldown middleware + store
  - `src/middleware/permissions.ts` — Permission checks
- `src/utils/` — Pure utilities (logger, embed, chart, retry, etc.)
- `src/config/` — Environment config, validation, and constants
- `src/types/` — TypeScript type definitions
- `src/locales/` — i18n translations (en, ja)
- `src/scripts/` — Utility scripts

## Layer Architecture

Each feature follows a layered structure:
- `commands/` — Slash command definitions (presentation layer, auto-loaded)
- `application/` — Business logic handlers (application layer)
- `repositories/` — Database access with real SQL queries (persistence layer)
- `services/` — External service integration, background jobs

`services/database/` is pure infrastructure: connection, transactions, and migrations only. All SQL queries live in feature repositories.

## Coding Standards

### Error Handling

- Always wrap command/event execution in try-catch
- Log errors with `logger.error()` — never use empty catch blocks
- Use `error instanceof Error ? error.message : error` pattern for safe logging
- Commands should reply with user-friendly error embeds, not raw error messages
- Use `process.on('unhandledRejection')` and `process.on('uncaughtException')` at the top level

### Database

- Use prepared statements for all queries (enforced by better-sqlite3)
- Use `runTransaction()` for operations that modify multiple tables
- Table names in dynamic queries must be validated against allowlists
- All table creation goes in `services/database/migrations/`
- SQL queries belong in feature `repositories/`, NOT in `services/database/`

### Voice

- Use the `entersState` + `Promise.race` pattern from `@discordjs/voice` for disconnect handling
- Always clean up audio buffers when disconnecting (`audioBufferManager.removeBuffer`)
- Respect `MAX_CONCURRENT_VC_CONNECTIONS` limit

### Services & Features

- Follow singleton pattern for service instances (export `const instance = new Service()`)
- Each feature module exports `{ name, start, stop }` from its `index.ts`
- Features are auto-discovered — no manual registration needed
- `startAllFeatures()` / `stopAllFeatures()` handle per-feature error isolation
- Health status is automatically tracked for each feature

### Localization

- Use `t(key, locale, params?)` for user-facing text
- Map Discord locales with `mapDiscordLocale(interaction.locale)`
- Add translations to both `en.ts` and `ja.ts`

### Testing

- Colocate tests with features: `features/<name>/__tests__/`
- Shared test helpers in `src/__tests__/helpers/`
- Integration tests in `src/__tests__/integration/`
- Use vitest with `vi.mock()` for module mocking
- Import mock Discord objects from `__tests__/helpers/discord.ts`

### File I/O

- Prefer `fs/promises` (async) over `fs` sync methods in async contexts
- Use `createWriteStream` for large file writes
- Sync methods (`existsSync`, `mkdirSync`) are acceptable only in constructors and module-level initialization
